    narr:narration """On 2026-08-20, the architecture hub carries a single decided migration: PostgreSQL to QuantumDB for the analytics pipeline, announced as settled fact by DaveQuantum. The decision is stated declaratively — [\"We're switching from PostgreSQL to QuantumDB for the analytics pipeline.\"](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1787217576351_1) — and restated in a [key-decisions bullet](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1787217576351_3) that compresses it to a one-liner. A [timeline pin](narr:Expr_1E2EQuantum1787217576351_5) commits the migration to Q3 2026, giving the decision a concrete future anchor. Two broader narratives sit beneath the hub: one frames this as a [database migration enacted as commitment](narr:Narrative_DatabaseMigrationDecision), the other as a [performance-and-cost justification](narr:Narrative_PerformanceCostRationale) — suggesting quantified benefits were marshaled to justify the architectural change, though the specific numbers are not present in the children under this hub. The conviction register across all three leaf segments is uniformly \"decision,\" and the temporal signature is concrete-irrealis-future: this is a settled change that has not yet happened. What is absent: any challenge, any dissent, any record of alternatives considered or rejected before QuantumDB was chosen.""" ;
